# Module Overview 

#### Thinking Critically About AI is organized around a set of **core ideas about how AI works and how humans should use it**. This professional learning module is structured to help you focus on the most important concepts and instructional moves, rather than walking lesson-by-lesson.

<div style="text-align: center; margin: 40px auto;"> 
  <img 
    src="https://images.code.org/84f21d55ad8a972bba224bf43dcca03b-image-1773419936950.jpg" 
    alt="A diagram showing the layout of the unit, with two lessons per milestone. Five milestones and ten lessons total." 
    style="width: 95%; height: auto; border-radius: 10px;">
</div>

## What's included in this module? 

#### This professional learning module is organized into **six sections**, each focused on a key idea or structure that supports student learning:

<div style="background-color: #FAFBFC; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 88%; margin: 20px auto;">

  <p style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0;">
    ⭐ Introduction to Thinking Critically About AI (You're here!)
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt;">
    This section orients you to the unit, including its structure, goals, and the role students take as AI testers and evaluators.
  </p>

  <br>

  <p style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
    🤖 Big Idea 1: AI is Powerful and Unreliable
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt;">
    You’ll explore how to help students understand how AI generates outputs based on patterns—not truth—and why it can sound convincing even when it is incorrect.
  </p>

  <br>

  <p style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
    🔍 Big Idea 2: AI Use Requires Testing & Evidence
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt;">
    You’ll learn how to guide students in systematically testing AI tools, collecting evidence, and identifying patterns in AI behavior.
  </p>

  <br>

  <p style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
    ⚖️ Big Idea 3: Context Matters
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt;">
    You’ll examine how to support students in making conditional judgments about when and how AI should be used based on the situation.
  </p>

  <br>

  <p style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
    🛡️ Big Idea 4: Responsible Use Includes Risk Awareness
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt;">
    You’ll explore how to guide students in recognizing risks related to privacy, bias, and misinformation, and how those risks influence responsible use.
  </p>

  <br>

  <p style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold;">
    🧩 Unit Project: Generate and Judge Guide
  </p>
  <p style="font-size: 13pt; margin-bottom: 0;">
    You’ll learn how the project develops across the unit and how to support students in building an evidence-based guide with clear recommendations for responsible AI use.
  </p>

</div>

___

#### This professional learning module is designed to prepare you to teach Thinking Critically About AI through its most important ideas and instructional moments. You can engage with the module in sections and return as needed to support your planning and instruction.
